  "description": "The PyroWave bitrate model as the host computes it. cases are at target_db, 35 dB, the author's default good quality, which the near figure (a television or monitor) uses. far_cases are at far_target_db, 31 dB, the handheld target the far figure (a device's own screen) uses, calibrated to one check by eye on a Retroid Pocket 6. tests/unit/test_pyrowave_advice.cpp holds Polaris to these rows. Nova's estimator ports the same header and mirrors both targets, and the two quote the same number for the same picture only while both evaluate the same header the same way at the same targets. Every mbps is the encoder's rate, before FEC, audio and overhead.",
